<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Highlight/P 11 0 R/F 4/M(D:20260815063856+02'00')/NM(a7e5eb76-94bb-4929-8efb-a69d8b9bfdf6)/Rect[ 43.374359 678.856254 564.309817 706.445313]/C[ 1 .819608 0]/Popup 531 0 R/T(Peter Gibson)/CA 1/CreationDate(D:20260815063225+02'00')/QuadPoints[ 46.348687 706.445313 561.335488 706.445313 46.348687 693.826307 561.335488 693.826307 46.348687 691.47526 522.70127 691.47526 46.348687 678.856254 522.70127 678.856254]/AP<</N 538 0 R>>/Contents(It is rare and even often impossible for a complaint to be part of a practical solution because fixing one failed feature like missing stair handrails cannot fix the lack of accessible lift so a person who can climb the stairs will be benefited but someone who cannot might not be able to go up due to the lift failure.  After build retrofit is often impractical.  Yes there is no valid justification but the complaint should be part of a practical solution which should be to stop future permissions for building which are inaccessible in the design stage.  Rejection of wrong designs should be the goal.)>>
